From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: pinetab2: let the camera use its
 internal AVDD regulator

Naming an avdd-supply makes ov5648_sensor_init() call

  ov5648_avdd_internal_power(sensor, !sensor->avdd)

which sets BP_REGULATOR_N in register 0x3013 and bypasses the sensor's own
analogue regulator in favour of the external rail. On the PineTab 2 that
leaves the analogue section unpowered: the digital side is perfect - the
built-in random-data pattern covers the full 10-bit range and the colour bar
pattern comes out pixel-exact with the bar edges at exact 240 pixel intervals
- while the pixel array reads out nothing but fixed column noise that does not
change when the sensor is covered or pointed somewhere else.

Clearing that bit by hand on a streaming sensor takes the frame mean from 49
to 636 out of 1023 and produces a normal image, so drop the supply and let the
sensor regulate AVDD itself.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
diff -ruN av_a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi av_b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi	2026-09-18 10:45:11.333839913 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi	2026-09-18 10:45:11.350647567 +0200
@@ -638,7 +638,15 @@
 		 */
 		power-domains = <&power RK3568_PD_VI>;
 
-		avdd-supply = <&vcc2v8_dvp>;
+		/*
+		 * No avdd-supply: naming one makes the driver bypass the
+		 * sensor's internal analogue regulator, and the analogue
+		 * section then stays dead on this board - the digital side
+		 * works perfectly (the built-in test patterns come out
+		 * pixel-exact) while the pixel array reads out nothing but
+		 * fixed column noise. Letting the sensor run its own
+		 * regulator takes the frame mean from 49 to 636.
+		 */
 		dvdd-supply = <&vdd1v2_dvp>;
 		dovdd-supply = <&vcc1v8_dvp>;
 		powerdown-gpios = <&gpio4 RK_PB2 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
